>Mahinda V was the last king of the Anuradhapura Kingdom in Sri Lanka, reigning from 982.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/mahipala-i-gurjara-pratihara"><span class="enc-name">Mahipala I (Gurjara-Pratihara)</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Mahipala I was king of the Gurjara-Pratihara dynasty of Kannauj in the early 10th century.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/mahipala-i-pala"><span class="enc-name">Mahipala I (Pala)</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Mahipala I was king of the Pala dynasty of Bengal and Bihar from about 988 to 1038.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/mahipala-i-pratihara"><span class="enc-name">Mahipala I (Pratihara)</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Mahipala I was a Gurjara-Pratihara emperor who ruled from Kannauj from about 913 to about 944.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/mahipala-ii"><span class="enc-name">Mahipala II</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Mahipala II was a king of the Pala dynasty of Bengal in the second half of the eleventh century.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/mahisagar-district"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/mahisagar-district.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Mahisagar district</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Mahisagar district is a district of eastern Gujarat, India, created in 2013 from parts of the Panchmahal and Kheda districts, with its headquarters at Lunavada.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/mahishmati"><span class="enc-name">Mahishmati</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Mahishmati was an ancient city on the Narmada river in central India, the southern capital of the kingdom of Avanti and later the seat of the